  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::1132",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is implicated in the interaction with Hrh4, which is involved in the regulation of G-protein coupled receptor activity. This activity is linked to Chrm4 through a series of molecular pathways, suggesting a potential role for Olanzapine in modulating cholinergic signaling. The evidence from both paths indicates that Olanzapine binds to Hrh4, which in turn participates in neurotransmitter receptor activity, ultimately influencing Chrm4. The overlapping pathways highlight a shared mechanism in which Olanzapine may affect cholinergic receptors by interacting with Hrh4, thereby altering receptor function. The integration of these pathways underscores a possible role for Olanzapine in the modulation of cholinergic signaling through Hrh4, providing a concise and mechanistically coherent explanation for its relationship with Chrm4.",
